The European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs, Kaja Kallas, said that Russia's increasing hybrid attacks, acts of sabotage, and stray drones are aimed at frightening the residents of European countries and deterring them from supporting Ukraine.
Kallas also acknowledges that the share of MEPs who openly argue that Ukraine should not be supported and that Russia poses no threat to Europe has grown.
